course: dictionary
lesson: 5017
title: Influence: a word with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Influence can be a noun or a verb, and the sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. As a noun, an influence is a person or thing that changes you: «Some cousins are a bad influence.» The sentence says saying no to something wrong is right, so a bad influence pulls you towards wrong choices.
explain: As a verb, to influence means to have an effect on someone or something. In a science lesson, we test what influences plant growth. Ask yourself: what changes here, and what makes it change? That is the influence.
explain: Read the words around influence for clues. «Under the influence» is a phrase meaning drunk or on drugs, and it appears in safety warnings about drinking and driving. Good, bad, and on are small clue words that show you the meaning.
fact: Influence (noun) means the power to change how someone thinks or acts, or how something happens.
fact: An influence is a person or thing that changes you, as in «She is a good influence.»
fact: To influence (verb) means to have an effect on someone or something.
fact: «Under the influence» is a phrase that means drunk or on drugs; it is used in safety warnings.
fact: Check a meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Adverts can influence what we buy» still makes sense if influence means to have an effect on.
exercise: «Some cousins are a bad influence.» What is an influence in this sentence? | *A person who changes how you act | A present for your birthday | A type of fruit | A loud noise at night
exercise: In a science lesson, we test what influences plant growth. What does influences mean here? | *Has an effect on | Writes about | Measures the height of | Stops
exercise: «Under the influence» means what? | Hiding under a table | Sleepy after lunch | *Drunk or on drugs | Very happy
test: «Old habits come back when you are bored or with the same friends.» What does this suggest about the same friends? | They are always late | They always make you laugh | They live far away | *They can pull you back to old habits
test: «Adverts can influence what we buy.» What does influence mean in this sentence? | To buy lots of things | To count the money | To be a shop | *To have an effect on what we buy
exam: In «they influenced Western civil service exams», what does influenced mean? | *Had an effect on | Ended | Paid for | Copied the words exactly
